& [SelectedIntention] is specify the complete M2 topology scanner before effect code
  + [purpose] is prove the entire candidate descendant topology safe for the initial mutation profile
  + [placement] is after fresh Phase3A receipt equality and before any writable App Server launch
  + [input] is exact candidate root, admission receipt digest and profile, scan profile, and hard limits
  + [output] is a single-use TopologyReceipt or a typed fail-closed fault

& [Profile] is cantor-windows-candidate-topology/0.1
  + [platform] is Windows desktop on a locally observed filesystem
  + [entries] are directories and regular files only
  + [reparse] every reparse point is rejected
  + [hard_link] every regular file with link count other than one is rejected
  + [identity] every duplicate strong file identity is rejected
  + [stream] every named data stream is rejected
  + [special] every device, socket-like, unknown, offline, recall-on-open, recall-on-data-access, or unsupported entry is rejected
  + [Git] nested repositories, nested .git entries, sparse checkout, submodules, and control drift are rejected

& [Completeness] is whole candidate not only allowed paths
  + [walk] is deterministic, no-follow, entry-before-descent, and resource-bounded
  + [ordering] is canonical relative path byte order
  + [records] include path, kind, attributes, identity, link count, stream facts, length, mode class, and content digest where applicable
  + [root] is included as an observed directory record
  + [boundary] excludes Git metadata as candidate content but separately proves its fixed control facts

& [StrongIdentity] is scan-local
  + [tuple] is volume serial plus 128-bit file identifier
  + [link_count] is obtained separately from the opened entry
  + [handle] is opened without following terminal reparse processing
  + [reuse] is never interpreted beyond the bounded scan

& [Freshness] is single use
  + [receipt] binds candidate root identity, Phase3A receipt digest, scan profile, policy digest, ordered inventory root, scan nonce supplied by caller, and result
  + [expiry] is any candidate observation or mutation mismatch, App Server launch attempt, elapsed freshness bound, or use attempt
  + [consumption] is exactly once by a matching MutationWorkPacket
  - never: reuse a receipt across jobs, roots, admission receipts, policies, or launches

& [Limits] are caller-declared and policy-bounded
  + [maximum_entries] is finite
  + [maximum_depth] is finite
  + [maximum_path_bytes] is finite
  + [maximum_file_bytes] is finite
  + [maximum_total_bytes] is finite
  + [maximum_streams_per_entry] is finite
  + [deadline] is explicit and monotonic
  = must: reject before exceeding any limit

& [Faults] are admission-denying
  + [topology_drift] is changed, vanished, replaced, or newly appeared entry
  + [alias] is reparse point, unexpected link count, or duplicate identity
  + [stream] is named, malformed, unbounded, or unobservable data stream
  + [special] is unsupported entry or attribute
  + [Git] is nested control, sparse, submodule, or control mismatch
  + [platform] is unsupported identity, stream, filesystem, encoding, or API behavior
  + [resource] is any hard bound
  + [OS] preserves operation and numeric error
  + [consequence] is no writable worker may launch and candidate state is unresolved if drift is possible

& [ImplementationSequence] is gated
  + [M2A] strict pure request, observation, policy, receipt, and fault forms
  + [M2B] target-specific windows-sys dependency and unsafe-seam review
  + [M2C] safe scanner plus confined read-only Windows adapter
  + [M2D] authorized synthetic adversarial fixtures and exact-boundary proof
  + [M2E] integration into fresh receipt revalidation and MutationWorkPacket

& [CurrentBoundary] is formation only
  + [allowed] is source preservation, SJS, canonical specification, exploded axes, justification, plan, requirement accounting, and research
  + [forbidden] is Cargo dependency change, unsafe, Win32 call, filesystem scan, fixture creation, link or stream creation, writable sandbox, App Server launch, mutation, seal, cleanup, Git publication of a candidate, and promotion
  - never: cite this source as implementation or execution authority

& [Acceptance] is P3TS-001 through P3TS-014
  + [P3TS-001] is whole-root deterministic no-follow inventory
  + [P3TS-002] is entry-before-descent reparse rejection
  + [P3TS-003] is 128-bit scan-local identity
  + [P3TS-004] is hard-link and duplicate-identity rejection
  + [P3TS-005] is complete named-stream accounting
  + [P3TS-006] is special and unsupported entry rejection
  + [P3TS-007] is nested Git and sparse-state rejection
  + [P3TS-008] is hard resource and deadline limits
  + [P3TS-009] is typed fail-closed OS and platform faults
  + [P3TS-010] is single-use receipt binding and expiry
  + [P3TS-011] is explicit non-atomic race boundary
  + [P3TS-012] is isolated generated Win32 binding proposal
  + [P3TS-013] is no authority leakage across M2 gates
  + [P3TS-014] is verification, evidence, rollback, and later integration closure
